ranch":"worktree-agent-a800707e77dae1b7a","clean":false,"head":"ee193375","history":[{"commit":"ee193375","summary":"wip(A33): one-command macOS build — tools/build-macos.sh (forks, standalone app, --package, --octosense host variant), tools/package-macos.sh (self-contained ad-hoc-signed OctosCode.app + zip: app-bundle profile with MAKEPAD=apple_bundle MAKEPAD_PACKAGE_DIR=makepad, every crate resources/ in the bundle), patches/octosense/0003-shell-octoscode-module.patch (the shell wiring + its additive Cargo.lock hunk) applied by prepare-octosense-fork.sh with a clear refusal for a hand-applied copy; docs/BUILD-macos.md, decision D10f; tests pin the scripts"},{"commit":"56c3da11","summary":"wip(A33): standalone OctosCode desktop app (crates/octoscode-desktop, binary octoscode) hosting the module like the OctoSense shell (own isolate, register+create in one trusted entry, root in the widget tree, drawn/fed inside the isolate); makepad from a patched fork (tools/prepare-makepad-fork.sh: 6cf03859 + patches/makepad/*, root [patch]); packaged-file-resource.patch (file_resource in a packaged build, failing-first makepad unit test); the kit faces back in the design embed (66c865ad dropped the ttf arm; failing-first design test); a packaged build never reads the build checkout"},{"commit":"9c4fb794","summary":"Merge A32: the two-dot ellipsis fixed in the shared path — makepad's layouter double-subtracted a soft-wrapped space and started the ellipsis inside the last kept glyph (and kept a centred row's pre-truncation offset): patches/makepad/layouter-ellipsis-pen.patch measures from the last glyph's end and re-aligns the row; the board-3 kit gives an under-measured single-line '…' label makepad's ellipsis too; failing-first (3/25 layouter tests, 44 kit runs past their label); sweep 220 makepad + 74 kit truncations, 0 two-dot endings; decision D10e (renumbered from the branch's D10d: the transport took D10d)"},{"commit":"08dc34a6","summary":"parity docs regenerated after A25's background attention (rows 276/322/323 still HELD; A 315 / B 43 / C 3)"},{"commit":"95291044","summary":"Merge A25 follow-up: background Sessions raise attention like the web — each background Session's own turns feed the tracker (its queued active turn, first pending interaction, latest real terminal), stopped / rate-limited never notify, a lost turn reads failed, one keyed OS notice per Session naming it, selecting acknowledges and withdraws; a25_notifications background phase; rows 276/322/323 stay HELD for the live macOS proof"},{"commit":"d586c614","summary":"Merge A22 follow-up: the transport never drops a reply (patches/octosense/0002: replies, error replies and connection states wait for room in the 64-slot event channel like notifications; a history read still unanswered after 20 s is logged, its queue reset and the Session re-opened once; failing-first flood test), and clicking the selected row of a Session whose history failed re-opens and re-reads it (was a dead control); D10d + the upstream PR draft"},{"commit":"976bbb21","summary":"replay skill-jobs: the second Session is a full id and the catalog read is attested (A22 row 228)"},{"commit":"92f16041","summary":"parity matrix regenerated after A24 phase 2 (A 315 / B 43 / C 3; 315 device-pending)"},{"commit":"3a23b385","summary":"fixture(A30 x A22 row 228): the --peer-dock catalog lists FULL Session ids and attests its scope; evidence on the merged build 50ca4300"},{"commit":"8faf8ccd","summary":"Merge A24 phase 2: the Chinese UI complete — the i18n bypass ceiling 314 -> 0 under a stricter scan (whole crate, string constants resolved, chips and pass-through helpers count), the native zh supplement (571 entries, second-reader reviewed, glossary-checked), the Fleet's status word and label shared with the peer dock (tests/a24_dock_words.rs, all 10 statuses, en + zh), the phone's Back closing the top surface like desktop Escape, the Skills job times in zh; rows 342/117 C->A"},{"commit":"0d3eaf9a","summary":"Phone: an inline surface boundary no longer swallows the open drawer's taps; the peer-dock fixture lists full Session ids"},{"commit":"afc60d8b","summary":"A32 evidence: the A29 marker state re-captured on the final clean host (merged with main) — 'Fix steer queue dro…' with three dots, desktop and phone, A29 walk 67/67 + 67/67; the trace sweeps (desktop, phone frames 300..368, the dialog family + peer dock walks): 220 truncation geometries and 74 kit-truncated texts, 0 two-dot or outside; 7 UX score rows (the marker row 8 -> 9)"}],"repo_root":"<PATH>","status":[{"code":"M","detail":"modified","path":"EADME.md"},{"code":"??","detail":"untracked","path":"docs/ux/a33/live-from-source/"},{"code":"??","detail":"untracked","path":"tools/walk/a33_other_mac_live.py"}]},"session_id":"dsflash:main","workspace":{"contract":["api octos-app-ui/v1alpha1","source session/open panes","feature pane.snapshots.v1"],"entries":[{"depth":0,"detail":"dir","kind":"directory","label":".octos","path":".octos"},{"depth":1,"detail":"7 B","kind":"file","label":"active-profile","path":".octos/active-profile"},{"depth":1,"detail":"dir","kind":"directory","label":"dsflash","path":".octos/dsflash"},{"depth":2,"detail":"191 B","kind":"file","label":".gitignore","path":".octos/dsflash/.gitignore"},{"depth":2,"detail":"dir","kind":"directory","label":"context_ledgers","path":".octos/dsflash/context_ledgers"},{"depth":3,"detail":"702 B","kind":"file","label":"dsflash%3Amain.json","path":".octos/dsflash/context_ledgers/dsflash%3Amain.json"},{"depth":2,"detail":"dir","kind":"directory","label":"sessions","path":".octos/dsflash/sessions"},{"depth":0,"detail":"4.7 KB","kind":"file","label":".octos-workspace.toml","path":".octos-workspace.toml"},{"depth":0,"detail":"31 B","kind":"file","label":"README.md","path":"README.md"}],"readable_roots":["<PATH>"],"root":"<PATH>","writable_roots":["<PATH>"]}},"session_id":"dsflash:main","workspace_root":"<PATH>"},"dir":"in","method":"session/open","wall_ms":1791000